      def generated_rule_sections
        [
          rule_section(:aim, GameRoomRules.translate("Liar's dice"),
            GameRoomRules.translate("Each player begins with 1\u20135 dice, normally five. Only you see your cup. A bid states how many dice of one face exist under all cups together. Raise the bid or challenge it. A false bid costs its bidder a die; challenging a true bid costs the challenger a die. A bid is true when at least the stated count exists. Players with no dice are eliminated. The last player with dice wins.")),
          rule_section(:variants, GameRoomRules.translate("Variants and exact calls"),
            GameRoomRules.translate("Classic uses no wilds. Raise the quantity, choosing any face, or keep the quantity and raise the face. Red Dead style adds Exactly: if the count is exact, every other player loses a die; otherwise the caller loses one. Perudo counts ones as wilds for other faces. A normal Perudo round cannot open on ones. Changing to ones requires half the last quantity rounded up; changing from ones requires double plus one. Increasing a bid of ones requires more ones.")),
          rule_section(:special, GameRoomRules.translate("Palifico, Calza and hidden rolls"),
            GameRoomRules.translate("Optional Perudo Palifico applies for one round when its starter first falls to one die and more than two players remain. Ones stop being wild; faces cannot change except for players who have already declared Palifico. Optional Calza lets anyone except the bidder claim an exact count before the next accepted bid. A correct Calza recovers one die up to the starting limit; an incorrect one loses a die. After a loss, the loser or next surviving seat starts. After successful Red Dead Exactly, the caller starts. After successful Calza, the last loser starts.")),
          rule_section(:privacy, GameRoomRules.translate("Private dice"),
            GameRoomRules.translate("Players first save secret commitments; the server then supplies a new random seed. Together these determine the hidden dice. Secrets are revealed and verified only after a challenge. Bots use their own cup and public bids. Keep the same Elten profile to retain your secrets. Saving or transferring a pending secret is blocked; an unrelated participant can still be replaced.")),
          rule_section(:controls, GameRoomRules.translate("Controls"),
            GameRoomRules.translate("Arrows and Enter choose a minimum legal bid for a face or a challenge. B opens a form for your own quantity and face. K calls bluff, D calls exactly when available. V reads your dice, L reads the current bid. Rolls and reveals happen through the shared executor automatically. F1 lists shortcuts; Ctrl+F1 opens rules. Chat, history and volume use shared controls."))
        ]
      end

